        {
          "path": "_m/w/9/s/r/puerto-princesa-wp/palawan-wildlife-rescue-and-co.jpg",
          "filename": "Palawan Wildlife Rescue and Conservation Center (9165480252).jpg",
          "caption": "Down time was very limited, so after check in, a quick ride into town to change currency (lucky an outlet of Western Union was open on a Sunday morning, though they gave a lousy rate!) and a quick bite, it was time for our afternoot tour of PP. I generally avoid bus tours, as they give you very little time in places you like to linger and spend more time in gift shops etc, but it was part of the package. Our first halt was the crocodile farm in PP, now called the Palawan Wildlife Rescue &amp; Conservation Centre. This is the signage at the entrance. (Puerto Princesa, Philippines, May 2013)",
          "alt": "Down time was very limited, so after check in, a quick ride into town to change currency (lucky an outlet of Western Union was open on a Sunday morning, though they gave a lousy rate!) and a quick bite, it was time for our afternoot tour of PP. I generally avoid bus tours, as they give you very little time in places you like to linger and spend more time in gift shops etc, but it was part of the package. Our first halt was the crocodile farm in PP, now called the Palawan Wildlife Rescue &amp; Conservation Centre. This is the signage at the entrance. (Puerto Princesa, Philippines, May 2013)",
